{"chunk_text":"The company is Google (Alphabet).

Evidence from TechCrunch [1] reports a class action lawsuit accusing Google and parent company Alphabet of anticompetitive behavior, including “siphoning off” news publishers’ content, readers, and ad revenue. The Age [2] discusses allegations that Google manipulates search queries for maximum ad revenue, and [3] notes critics contend Google manipulates Search to maximize ad revenue. TechCrunch [4] and [6] further describe Google’s AI-based search and Featured Snippets as shifting traffic away from publishers, and [8] mentions Google “starving the free press.”
Answer: Google","is_final":true}
